score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":1.0,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":100.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.31171694594940186,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":100.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":1.1211606282586883,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":0.09214904357904985,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":100.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.004043769711598085,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":15.6,"_gate_share_shrink":0.1165316992018508,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.12314668720158765,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.29228002,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.8,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":80.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Nutex Health Inc. operates as a healthcare services and operations company in the United States. It operates through three segments: Hospital, Population Health Management (PHM), and Real Estate. The Hospital segment develops and operates a network of micro hospitals, specialty hospitals, and hospital outpatient departments that offer healthcare services, including emergency room care, inpatient care, and behavioural health. It also provides imaging services, such as CT scan, X-ray, MRI, ultrasound, etc.; laboratory services; and onsite inpatient pharmacies. The PHM segment provides management, administrative, and other support services to its affiliated hospitals and physician groups by establishing and operating provider networks, such as independent physician associations (IPAs); and a cloud-based technology platform for IPAs. The Real Estate segment owns and leases land and hospital buildings. Nutex Health Inc. was founded in 2011 and is headquartered in Houston, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Thomas T. Vo M.B.A., M.D. | Chairman of the Board & CEO | Age 52 | Compensation: $1.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 944 people. Revenue per employee of $927K ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, improving at 56%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $260K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $114K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Nutex Health Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.2B market cap on $875M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +59% over the past three years and +112% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +6.6pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -14% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 43%.","The business throws off $246M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 28 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.51\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","Accruals are elevated at -19.3% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 12\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.4%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 12% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 29% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 3.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (28.6% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 31% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 34% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 78% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Growing faster than most Healthcare peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Financial quality scores above most Healthcare peers","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Nutex Health (NUTX) Reports Mixed Earnings, Is A 32% Discount Still Justified?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/healthcare/nasdaq-nutx/nutex-health/news/nutex-health-nutx-reports-mixed-earnings-is-a-32-discount-st","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793993034.408,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.84,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"(NUTX) Movement Within Algorithmic Entry Frameworks","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/89/NUTX_Movement_Within_Algorithmic_Entry_Frameworks_110626021002_1793992202.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793992202.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Nutex Health Inc. (NUTX) Q3 Earnings and Revenues Beat Estimates","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3024843/nutex-health-inc-nutx-q3-earnings-and-revenues-beat-estimates?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_4-3024843","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793913603.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Why (NUTX) Price Action Is Critical for Tactical Trading","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/12/Why_NUTX_Price_Action_Is_Critical_for_Tactical_Trading_102726022802_1793125682.html","date":"2026-10-27","timestamp":1793125682.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.557,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Nutex Health (NASDAQ:NUTX) Shares Gap Down \u2013 What\u2019s Next?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/09/nutex-health-nasdaqnutx-shares-gap-down-whats-next.html","date":"2026-10-09","timestamp":1791560473.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.915,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Nutex Health Q3 Earnings Call Highlights","source":"thel